
Provider is behind one interface, `DocumentAssistant`. The rest of the app does not call a vendor SDK directly.
---
## 13. Media, watermark, social
- Accept JPEG, PNG, WEBP, MP4, and MP3. Max image 20 MB, video 200 MB, audio 30 MB.
- Store originals in a private bucket. Clients receive short-lived signed URLs.
- Generate a preview image for photos and video posters. Watermark when the rule in section 7 says so. Do this in a background job, not in the request.
- Videos are not re-encoded with a burned-in mark in version one. A poster image is watermarked and playback of preview-only video uses a visible overlay. State that limitation in the UI.
- Social connect, phase 5: OAuth where the provider allows a public profile read. On success, store URL, display name, and avatar only if the artist confirms the import. Do not post, like, or message on their behalf. Do not request publish permissions.
- If a provider denies the app, the manual URL field still works. Profile completeness treats a manual URL as done.
