## 15. Non-functional requirements
- Search and profile pages respond in under 500 ms at the server for a warm cache, excluding media bytes.
- Payment webhook processing is idempotent and safe to retry.
- Authorized users can read only their inquiries, bookings, messages, and private media.
- Public profiles expose no email, phone, exact home address, or original file key.
- Rate-limit auth, inquiry creation, chat send, and AI routes.
- Timezones are stored on the event. Never store a bare local time.
- Dates in the UI use the event timezone and also show the viewer's local zone when they differ.
- Accessibility: form labels, contrast, keyboard use on web, captions not required on user videos in version one.
- Audit fields on quote acceptance, deal-sheet acceptance, payment status changes, and checklist checks: user id, timestamp, IP.
### Scale assumption for the first production layout
Design for 10,000 artist profiles, 100,000 inquiries, and short chat threads. Do not build microservices, sharding, or a custom CDN. Do keep the API stateless so a second instance is a config change.
