## 20. First instruction to the coding model
Implement Phase 1 and the repo skeleton for later phases. Create the monorepo, auth, roles, artist profile, public search and profile, travel flag, availability, inquiry chat, and private media with watermarked previews. Include PostgreSQL migrations, seed data for one artist and one booker, and tests for: contact privacy, travel flag required, and preview vs original URL.
Do not implement payments, AI, checklists, or social OAuth until Phase 1 acceptance checks pass. Leave the database tables for Quote, Booking, DealSheet, and Payment in migrations so later phases do not reshape identity, but do not expose their UI yet.
When Phase 1 passes, continue in order through Phase 5 using the acceptance checks in section 18 as the definition of done.
